        "created_at": "2013-09-18T00:09:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Reckless\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/48/2467_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Reckless:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Starsaber wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Reckless wrote:<br><blockquote>&nbsp;awp832 wrote:<br><blockquote>Essentially the only cards that are destroyed when an identical card is played are the hero cards that have the \"Limited\" tag.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nAdditional copies of Limited cards in play are actually immediately discarded rather when they are played, according to the rulebook.&nbsp; It means that characters like Ra cannot play a second copy of his Staff, regain three HP, and have it blow up.\n</blockquote>\n&nbsp;But you can use its power that destroys it and play the new one the next turn to heal.\n</blockquote></div>\nYes.&nbsp; That is definitely something you can do.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>A pity that Fanatic can't throw her sword.</p>",
